# mkdocs documentation
#
# /site used to be ignored here. That rule arrives with the standard Python
# gitignore and means "mkdocs build output", which this repository has never
# had: nothing here uses mkdocs. What /site does hold is the companion site
# for lab.nexagenlabs.com, written by hand and committed on purpose, and the
# inherited rule made the whole folder invisible to git.
#
# If mkdocs is ever added, give it a different output directory rather than
# restoring this line. The thirteen URLs printed in the book resolve through
# site/_redirects, and a build tool silently overwriting or hiding that file
# would take every one of them down with it.

