# Session scratchpad. Claude writes its report here for a human to read, and
# its claims go stale the moment the session ends. Committed across twelve
# builds it would accumulate a dozen contradictory assertions about the state
# of the repository, which is a small version of the failure this project is
# about. The durable record is the commit history and the gates.
HANDOFF.md
HANDOFF.previous.md

# tools/verify_printed_urls.py writes these. They record what was live at one
# moment, so they are stale the moment they are written, and a committed copy
# would have the repository asserting something it cannot know is still true.
# Run the tool to get a current one. The reference reports are different and
# are committed, because they check data that lives in this repository.
printed_urls_report.md
printed_urls_report.json

# Written by any stage file or agent.py that is actually run: one JSONL trace
# per run. Useful to read, never to commit.
runs/
